1
00:00:00,112 --> 00:00:01,549
The boat drifts for an hour

2
00:00:01,549 --> 00:00:03,800
before either of you picks up an oar.

3
00:00:04,222 --> 00:00:06,687
Slabs of ice turn slowly around you,

4
00:00:06,687 --> 00:00:09,813
and knock against the hull, and drift on.

5
00:00:09,813 --> 00:00:11,828
Above you, there's nothing.

6
00:00:12,235 --> 00:00:13,391
No straight edge.

7
00:00:13,391 --> 00:00:15,553
No dark wall on the horizon.

8
00:00:15,992 --> 00:00:18,962
Just sky, a pale winter blue,

9
00:00:18,962 --> 00:00:21,289
from one side of the world to the other.

10
00:00:21,289 --> 00:00:23,493
You keep looking up anyway.

11
00:00:23,493 --> 00:00:25,062
After a hundred and eighty days,

12
00:00:25,062 --> 00:00:27,889
your neck has forgotten how to stop.

13
00:00:27,889 --> 00:00:29,186
Then the cold reminds you

14
00:00:29,186 --> 00:00:30,783
of something more urgent.

15
00:00:31,316 --> 00:00:32,460
One match.

16
00:00:32,460 --> 00:00:33,763
No fire steel.

17
00:00:33,763 --> 00:00:36,815
Two tins, and one bag of flour.

18
00:00:36,815 --> 00:00:39,128
A sky with nothing in it

19
00:00:39,128 --> 00:00:40,852
won't keep you warm tonight.

20
00:00:40,852 --> 00:00:41,565
So you row,

21
00:00:41,565 --> 00:00:44,350
slowly, downstream, to the village.

22
00:00:44,350 --> 00:00:46,460
The main street is silent.

23
00:00:46,866 --> 00:00:48,844
The units still stand along it,

24
00:00:48,844 --> 00:00:50,195
dark and smooth,

25
00:00:50,553 --> 00:00:53,649
and when you step onto the road, nothing lights.

26
00:00:53,649 --> 00:00:55,517
Not the nearest pair.

27
00:00:55,517 --> 00:00:56,351
Not the next.

28
00:00:56,351 --> 00:00:58,734
The lights don't want you anymore.

29
00:00:59,381 --> 00:01:00,553
You go into the first

30
00:01:00,553 --> 00:01:01,885
house with an open door.

31
00:01:01,885 --> 00:01:03,010
In the kitchen,

32
00:01:03,010 --> 00:01:06,682
there's a wood stove, a basket of logs, and a drawer.

33
00:01:07,024 --> 00:01:09,465
In the drawer, there's a lighter.

34
00:01:09,465 --> 00:01:11,549
And two full boxes of matches.

35
00:01:11,549 --> 00:01:13,180
Mara laughs so hard she

36
00:01:13,180 --> 00:01:15,441
has to sit down on the floor.

37
00:01:15,441 --> 00:01:17,718
In the pantry, there's a jar of jam,

38
00:01:17,718 --> 00:01:19,743
a bag of rice, and a row of tins

39
00:01:19,743 --> 00:01:21,670
with their labels facing out,

40
00:01:21,670 --> 00:01:24,222
the way somebody tidy would leave them.

41
00:01:24,755 --> 00:01:26,227
You eat jam with a spoon,

42
00:01:26,227 --> 00:01:28,566
straight from the jar, standing up.

43
00:01:28,923 --> 00:01:30,129
Nobody stops you.

44
00:01:30,129 --> 00:01:32,341
There's nobody left to stop you.

45
00:01:32,341 --> 00:01:34,917
You light the stove with the lighter.

46
00:01:34,917 --> 00:01:36,623
The last match from your old box,

47
00:01:36,623 --> 00:01:38,684
you put back in your pocket.

48
00:01:38,684 --> 00:01:41,010
It came all the way from the narrowboat.

49
00:01:41,010 --> 00:01:42,048
It can stay.

50
00:01:42,630 --> 00:01:44,739
That night, you sleep in a real bed,

51
00:01:44,739 --> 00:01:46,401
under real blankets,

52
00:01:46,401 --> 00:01:48,467
in a house where nobody is coming back.

53
00:01:48,467 --> 00:01:49,707
It's the warmest you've

54
00:01:49,707 --> 00:01:51,605
been since the station.

55
00:01:51,605 --> 00:01:53,595
You don't sleep at all.

56
00:01:53,595 --> 00:01:54,571
On day 183,

57
00:01:54,571 --> 00:01:56,296
you walk through the whole village.

58
00:01:56,296 --> 00:01:57,111
It takes an hour,

59
00:01:57,111 --> 00:01:59,075
because you go into every house.

60
00:01:59,075 --> 00:02:00,538
They're all the same.

61
00:02:00,538 --> 00:02:03,078
On every front door, at the height of a hand,

62
00:02:03,078 --> 00:02:05,080
there's the mark you saw before.

63
00:02:05,422 --> 00:02:07,828
Two circles, joined by a short line.

64
00:02:07,828 --> 00:02:09,258
Behind every door,

65
00:02:09,258 --> 00:02:11,867
beds are made, and coats hang on their hooks.

66
00:02:11,867 --> 00:02:14,956
In one kitchen, two plates sit on the table,

67
00:02:14,956 --> 00:02:16,131
washed and dried,

68
00:02:16,131 --> 00:02:18,760
as if somebody meant to come back for dinner.

69
00:02:18,760 --> 00:02:20,339
The bags are gone.

70
00:02:20,339 --> 00:02:21,747
People took what they carried.

71
00:02:21,747 --> 00:02:23,273
They left everything else.

72
00:02:23,728 --> 00:02:25,462
In a child's bedroom, a row of toy

73
00:02:25,462 --> 00:02:27,727
cars is lined up on the windowsill,

74
00:02:27,727 --> 00:02:30,126
all facing the same way, toward the square.

75
00:02:30,126 --> 00:02:31,919
You don't touch them.

76
00:02:31,919 --> 00:02:34,036
The pantries haven't been touched.

77
00:02:34,036 --> 00:02:36,107
Tins, rice, pasta, jars of jam.

78
00:02:36,107 --> 00:02:38,646
More food than you've seen in one place

79
00:02:38,646 --> 00:02:40,766
since the first inventory at the station.

80
00:02:40,766 --> 00:02:42,339
You count it anyway.

81
00:02:42,339 --> 00:02:43,945
It takes all afternoon.

82
00:02:43,945 --> 00:02:45,216
Mara doesn't help.

83
00:02:45,216 --> 00:02:47,337
She sits on the steps of the church,

84
00:02:47,337 --> 00:02:48,545
looking at the square.

85
00:02:48,545 --> 00:02:49,717
In the middle of it,

86
00:02:49,717 --> 00:02:52,951
there's a ring on the cobbles, a wide circle of faint,

87
00:02:52,951 --> 00:02:55,353
dark lines where the light used to be.

88
00:02:55,353 --> 00:02:56,542
She walks into it,

89
00:02:56,542 --> 00:02:58,594
and stands there, in the middle.

90
00:02:58,594 --> 00:02:59,684
Nothing happens.

91
00:02:59,684 --> 00:03:01,271
Nothing lights.

92
00:03:01,271 --> 00:03:02,479
Nothing comes down.

93
00:03:02,479 --> 00:03:04,702
She says she wanted to know what it

94
00:03:04,702 --> 00:03:07,074
felt like to stand where they stood.

95
00:03:07,074 --> 00:03:09,223
You ask what it feels like.

96
00:03:09,223 --> 00:03:10,581
She says it feels like a

97
00:03:10,581 --> 00:03:12,672
bus stop after the last bus.

98
00:03:12,672 --> 00:03:14,238
You write it in the ledger.

99
00:03:14,238 --> 00:03:15,601
Everybody went up.

100
00:03:16,007 --> 00:03:19,347
Then, after a long time, you add one word.

101
00:03:19,347 --> 00:03:20,268
Almost.

102
00:03:20,738 --> 00:03:24,181
On day 186, Mara finds the square.

103
00:03:24,587 --> 00:03:25,801
She's been looking at the

104
00:03:25,801 --> 00:03:27,670
plain figure's last drawing every night,

105
00:03:27,670 --> 00:03:29,656
by the light of the stove.

106
00:03:29,656 --> 00:03:31,077
The ship, going up.

107
00:03:31,403 --> 00:03:32,739
Sixty short lines.

108
00:03:32,739 --> 00:03:35,042
An arrow, pointing down.

109
00:03:35,578 --> 00:03:37,404
Tonight, she holds the roll right

110
00:03:37,404 --> 00:03:39,431
up to the flame, and goes very quiet.

111
00:03:39,431 --> 00:03:40,798
At the tip of the arrow,

112
00:03:40,798 --> 00:03:42,985
there's something you missed.

113
00:03:42,985 --> 00:03:43,867
A tiny square.

114
00:03:43,867 --> 00:03:46,048
You've seen that square before.

115
00:03:46,761 --> 00:03:48,838
On day 69, at the start of the map,

116
00:03:48,838 --> 00:03:50,223
the plain figure drew a

117
00:03:50,223 --> 00:03:51,986
small square for the station.

118
00:03:51,986 --> 00:03:54,312
That's where the arrow points.

119
00:03:54,312 --> 00:03:57,347
On day 240, the ship is coming back.

120
00:03:57,347 --> 00:03:59,248
To the gas station.

121
00:03:59,248 --> 00:04:02,003
To the exact place where it all started,

122
00:04:02,003 --> 00:04:04,255
on the evening you tried to pay for milk.

123
00:04:04,255 --> 00:04:06,054
You argue about it for three days.

124
00:04:06,054 --> 00:04:07,800
You say away from the ship.

125
00:04:07,800 --> 00:04:10,485
It's been your answer since day five.

126
00:04:10,485 --> 00:04:12,800
Mara says she isn't asking to go up.

127
00:04:12,800 --> 00:04:14,543
She's asking to see it coming,

128
00:04:14,543 --> 00:04:16,736
for once, instead of running from it.

129
00:04:17,174 --> 00:04:18,575
And somewhere up there is the

130
00:04:18,575 --> 00:04:20,649
only one of them who ever waved back.

131
00:04:21,087 --> 00:04:22,002
On the third night,

132
00:04:22,002 --> 00:04:25,535
you stop arguing, because you realize you agree with her.

133
00:04:25,535 --> 00:04:26,524
You've spent a hundred and

134
00:04:26,524 --> 00:04:28,350
eighty-six days being surprised.

135
00:04:28,869 --> 00:04:30,873
You'd like to be ready, just once.

136
00:04:30,873 --> 00:04:33,379
In a garden shed, you find a child's

137
00:04:33,379 --> 00:04:35,496
wooden sled with a rope on the front.

138
00:04:35,496 --> 00:04:36,511
Fifty-one days.

139
00:04:36,511 --> 00:04:38,148
That's long enough to walk home.

140
00:04:38,148 --> 00:04:39,140
You've never called

141
00:04:39,140 --> 00:04:40,680
the station home before.

142
00:04:41,006 --> 00:04:43,678
You notice that you just did.

143
00:04:43,678 --> 00:04:45,020
On day 189,

144
00:04:45,020 --> 00:04:46,664
you leave the village with the sled.

145
00:04:46,664 --> 00:04:47,953
You load it the way you used

146
00:04:47,953 --> 00:04:48,979
to load your bags,

147
00:04:48,979 --> 00:04:51,389
which means you count everything twice.

148
00:04:51,844 --> 00:04:52,848
Twenty-six tins.

149
00:04:52,848 --> 00:04:54,633
Three bags of rice.

150
00:04:54,633 --> 00:04:56,472
Two bags of pasta.

151
00:04:56,472 --> 00:04:57,856
One jar of jam.

152
00:04:57,856 --> 00:05:00,487
Two lighters, three boxes of matches,

153
00:05:00,487 --> 00:05:03,069
and one very old match in your pocket.

154
00:05:03,412 --> 00:05:05,772
The kettle, the blankets, the tin.

155
00:05:05,772 --> 00:05:06,851
And the red can,

156
00:05:06,851 --> 00:05:08,691
tied to the back of the sled,

157
00:05:08,691 --> 00:05:11,119
because by now it would be rude to leave it.

158
00:05:11,119 --> 00:05:13,590
You walk upstream, along the bank.

159
00:05:13,590 --> 00:05:15,802
By noon, you reach the mill.

160
00:05:15,802 --> 00:05:17,899
It looks smaller than you remember.

161
00:05:18,273 --> 00:05:19,317
In the loft window,

162
00:05:19,317 --> 00:05:21,404
there's a puddle of white wax where the

163
00:05:21,404 --> 00:05:23,379
last candle burned itself out.

164
00:05:23,379 --> 00:05:24,996
Nobody blew it out.

165
00:05:25,338 --> 00:05:26,355
Nobody needed to.

166
00:05:26,355 --> 00:05:28,870
The wheel is still locked in ice.

167
00:05:28,870 --> 00:05:30,270
The channel you opened has

168
00:05:30,270 --> 00:05:32,333
frozen over again, thin and gray.

169
00:05:32,723 --> 00:05:34,814
Around the island, there's no ring at all.

170
00:05:34,814 --> 00:05:36,400
At the edge of the channel,

171
00:05:36,400 --> 00:05:39,060
half buried in snow, you find the marker.

172
00:05:39,627 --> 00:05:41,771
Two circles, joined by a short line.

173
00:05:41,771 --> 00:05:43,966
It's the size of your hand,

174
00:05:43,966 --> 00:05:46,691
and dark, and much heavier than it looks.

175
00:05:46,691 --> 00:05:47,693
It doesn't glow.

176
00:05:47,693 --> 00:05:48,930
Mara picks it up and

177
00:05:48,930 --> 00:05:50,556
holds it for a long time.

178
00:05:50,556 --> 00:05:52,247
Then she wraps it in a scarf

179
00:05:52,247 --> 00:05:54,042
from the village and puts it

180
00:05:54,042 --> 00:05:55,711
in the tin, with the ledger.

181
00:05:55,711 --> 00:05:56,990
Already counted.

182
00:05:57,364 --> 00:05:58,450
Leave these two.

183
00:05:58,450 --> 00:05:59,392
You walk on.

184
00:05:59,392 --> 00:06:02,157
Behind you, the mill gets small,

185
00:06:02,157 --> 00:06:04,722
and then it's gone behind the trees.

186
00:06:04,722 --> 00:06:05,854
On day 192,

187
00:06:05,854 --> 00:06:07,456
you sleep at the cottage again.

188
00:06:07,456 --> 00:06:09,722
The boathouse is empty, of course.

189
00:06:09,722 --> 00:06:11,181
The garden is under snow,

190
00:06:11,181 --> 00:06:14,722
but Mara digs anyway, the way she did on day 100.

191
00:06:14,722 --> 00:06:15,997
Three small potatoes.

192
00:06:15,997 --> 00:06:18,590
She holds them up like trophies,

193
00:06:18,590 --> 00:06:21,179
and honestly, after everything, they are.

194
00:06:21,649 --> 00:06:23,571
From the cottage, you find the stream,

195
00:06:23,571 --> 00:06:25,899
and follow it uphill, on the bank this time.

196
00:06:25,899 --> 00:06:27,744
Your feet still remember the water.

197
00:06:27,744 --> 00:06:29,837
They don't want to go back in.

198
00:06:29,837 --> 00:06:30,559
It's strange,

199
00:06:30,559 --> 00:06:32,561
walking your own story backward.

200
00:06:32,886 --> 00:06:35,096
The fallen tree where you slept,

201
00:06:35,096 --> 00:06:36,034
back to back.

202
00:06:36,034 --> 00:06:38,701
The bend where you checked your soles,

203
00:06:38,701 --> 00:06:39,744
and they were dark.

204
00:06:39,744 --> 00:06:41,279
Every place looks smaller.

205
00:06:41,279 --> 00:06:43,554
Every place looks safer than it felt.

206
00:06:43,927 --> 00:06:46,075
You eat the potatoes baked in the embers,

207
00:06:46,075 --> 00:06:46,637
with salt,

208
00:06:46,637 --> 00:06:49,350
and they taste exactly like day 100.

209
00:06:49,350 --> 00:06:51,341
That night, by a fire you light

210
00:06:51,341 --> 00:06:52,676
without counting the matches,

211
00:06:52,676 --> 00:06:54,578
you read the ledger from the start.

212
00:06:54,903 --> 00:06:55,879
Forty minutes.

213
00:06:55,879 --> 00:06:56,935
Closed room.

214
00:06:56,935 --> 00:06:58,683
Safe behind the wall.

215
00:06:58,683 --> 00:07:00,412
They notice what changes.

216
00:07:00,412 --> 00:07:03,030
You were wrong about almost everything,

217
00:07:03,030 --> 00:07:03,644
at first.

218
00:07:03,644 --> 00:07:05,895
But you wrote it all down.

219
00:07:05,895 --> 00:07:07,655
And it's the only reason

220
00:07:07,655 --> 00:07:09,768
you're still here to read it.

221
00:07:09,768 --> 00:07:11,828
On day 195, you see smoke.

222
00:07:11,828 --> 00:07:12,719
A thin gray line,

223
00:07:12,719 --> 00:07:15,610
rising from the chimney of an old stone schoolhouse,

224
00:07:15,610 --> 00:07:17,769
on a hill above the stream.

225
00:07:17,769 --> 00:07:19,135
Someone else made it.

226
00:07:19,135 --> 00:07:21,667
You watch it for an hour, the old way.

227
00:07:21,667 --> 00:07:23,609
Then Mara walks up the track,

228
00:07:23,609 --> 00:07:26,519
in plain view, and knocks on the door.

229
00:07:26,519 --> 00:07:28,153
The door opens a crack.

230
00:07:28,153 --> 00:07:29,782
Four faces look out at you.

231
00:07:29,782 --> 00:07:30,770
An older couple,

232
00:07:30,770 --> 00:07:33,677
gray-haired, and a younger pair behind them.

233
00:07:33,677 --> 00:07:35,445
They didn't follow the lights either.

234
00:07:35,445 --> 00:07:37,776
They hid in the cellar every time

235
00:07:37,776 --> 00:07:39,766
a circle lit up near the school,

236
00:07:39,766 --> 00:07:40,652
for a hundred and ninety-five days.

237
00:07:40,652 --> 00:07:43,101
They keep hens in the old playground.

238
00:07:43,101 --> 00:07:44,384
You haven't seen an

239
00:07:44,384 --> 00:07:46,047
egg since before the ship.

240
00:07:46,047 --> 00:07:48,585
You trade six tins for a dozen eggs,

241
00:07:48,585 --> 00:07:50,989
and it's the best trade you've ever made.

242
00:07:50,989 --> 00:07:52,505
The older woman cooks four of

243
00:07:52,505 --> 00:07:54,329
them in a black pan on the range,

244
00:07:54,329 --> 00:07:56,256
and watches you eat them as if

245
00:07:56,256 --> 00:07:58,564
she's never seen anyone so hungry.

246
00:07:58,564 --> 00:08:00,539
She probably hasn't.

247
00:08:00,539 --> 00:08:02,818
In a hundred and ninety-five days,

248
00:08:02,818 --> 00:08:04,928
you're the first people who knocked.

249
00:08:04,928 --> 00:08:07,942
Over supper, you show them the ledger.

250
00:08:07,942 --> 00:08:09,349
The rows of seats.

251
00:08:09,349 --> 00:08:10,164
The arrow.

252
00:08:10,164 --> 00:08:11,130
Day 240.

253
00:08:11,712 --> 00:08:13,889
The older man listens politely.

254
00:08:13,889 --> 00:08:15,955
Then he says the ship is gone,

255
00:08:15,955 --> 00:08:17,614
and that's the end of it.

256
00:08:17,614 --> 00:08:19,555
The schoolhouse has walls,

257
00:08:19,555 --> 00:08:21,434
food, and a cellar.

258
00:08:21,743 --> 00:08:23,087
Staying seems obvious.

259
00:08:23,087 --> 00:08:24,724
You've thought that before.

260
00:08:24,724 --> 00:08:26,279
You don't argue.

261
00:08:26,279 --> 00:08:27,376
You know exactly how

262
00:08:27,376 --> 00:08:29,608
convincing it looks from the inside.

263
00:08:30,302 --> 00:08:31,212
In the morning,

264
00:08:31,212 --> 00:08:33,542
the younger woman walks you to the gate.

265
00:08:33,542 --> 00:08:34,554
She asks,

266
00:08:34,554 --> 00:08:37,901
quietly, what you'll do on day 240.

267
00:08:37,901 --> 00:08:40,145
Mara says: be there.

268
00:08:40,145 --> 00:08:42,609
On day 198, the lights wake up.

269
00:08:42,609 --> 00:08:44,314
You're walking along a country

270
00:08:44,314 --> 00:08:45,085
road at dusk,

271
00:08:45,085 --> 00:08:48,149
the sled hissing behind you on the last of the snow.

272
00:08:48,149 --> 00:08:49,847
Units stand along the verge,

273
00:08:49,847 --> 00:08:53,146
dark, the way they've been since the ship left.

274
00:08:53,146 --> 00:08:55,841
Then every single one of them lights up.

275
00:08:55,841 --> 00:08:56,977
At once.

276
00:08:56,977 --> 00:08:58,012
Joined circles,

277
00:08:58,012 --> 00:09:00,898
glowing pale at every base, along the road,

278
00:09:00,898 --> 00:09:04,591
across the fields, on roads you can't even see,

279
00:09:04,591 --> 00:09:06,372
all the way to the horizon.

280
00:09:06,372 --> 00:09:07,325
For three seconds,

281
00:09:07,325 --> 00:09:10,280
the whole country is lit up like a map.

282
00:09:10,280 --> 00:09:12,008
Then it all goes dark again.

283
00:09:12,008 --> 00:09:13,999
You stand in the road with

284
00:09:13,999 --> 00:09:15,638
your heart going like a hammer.

285
00:09:15,638 --> 00:09:17,993
Mara doesn't say anything for a long time.

286
00:09:17,993 --> 00:09:20,277
Then she says it looked like someone

287
00:09:20,277 --> 00:09:23,096
testing the lights in a house before a party.

288
00:09:23,096 --> 00:09:24,686
You hope she's wrong.

289
00:09:25,302 --> 00:09:26,465
You know she isn't.

290
00:09:26,465 --> 00:09:28,500
You count the days on your fingers,

291
00:09:28,500 --> 00:09:31,941
because the map is at the bottom of the bag.

292
00:09:31,941 --> 00:09:32,617
Forty-two.

293
00:09:32,617 --> 00:09:33,691
Forty-two days,

294
00:09:33,691 --> 00:09:36,576
and the lights are already practicing.

295
00:09:36,935 --> 00:09:38,375
You think of the schoolhouse

296
00:09:38,375 --> 00:09:39,815
on the hill, and the cellar,

297
00:09:39,815 --> 00:09:41,781
and the older man saying it's over.

298
00:09:41,781 --> 00:09:44,288
You hope they were looking the other way.

299
00:09:44,743 --> 00:09:45,434
That night,

300
00:09:45,434 --> 00:09:48,208
you camp away from the road, with no fire.

301
00:09:48,744 --> 00:09:49,447
Out of habit,

302
00:09:49,447 --> 00:09:51,501
you leave the lighter in your pocket.

303
00:09:51,501 --> 00:09:53,041
Some habits are earned.

304
00:09:53,041 --> 00:09:54,515
The sky stays empty.

305
00:09:54,515 --> 00:09:57,233
But you watch it all night anyway.

306
00:09:57,233 --> 00:09:58,560
You write in the ledger.

307
00:09:58,560 --> 00:10:00,081
They're getting ready.

308
00:10:00,488 --> 00:10:03,841
Underneath, Mara writes: so are we.

309
00:10:04,328 --> 00:10:05,141
On day 201,

310
00:10:05,141 --> 00:10:07,954
it rains, and the snow goes away.

311
00:10:08,505 --> 00:10:11,037
All of it, in one gray, dripping day.

312
00:10:11,037 --> 00:10:13,016
The sled stops hissing,

313
00:10:13,016 --> 00:10:14,273
and starts scraping.

314
00:10:14,273 --> 00:10:15,350
By the afternoon,

315
00:10:15,350 --> 00:10:17,714
it's dragging through mud, and you leave it

316
00:10:17,714 --> 00:10:19,853
under a hedge at the foot of the hill.

317
00:10:20,210 --> 00:10:21,531
You carry the bags.

318
00:10:21,531 --> 00:10:22,983
Mara carries the can.

319
00:10:22,983 --> 00:10:24,340
It isn't heavy.

320
00:10:24,697 --> 00:10:26,636
She just doesn't trust it alone.

321
00:10:26,636 --> 00:10:28,399
At the top of the hill,

322
00:10:28,399 --> 00:10:29,870
the sheepfold is waiting.

323
00:10:29,870 --> 00:10:31,764
The ring of dry stone.

324
00:10:31,764 --> 00:10:33,008
The narrow opening.

325
00:10:33,008 --> 00:10:34,874
The flat stone in the middle.

326
00:10:34,874 --> 00:10:36,855
The band around it is gone.

327
00:10:36,855 --> 00:10:38,551
Outside the wall, in the wet grass,

328
00:10:38,551 --> 00:10:41,250
you find a small, brown, shriveled thing.

329
00:10:41,250 --> 00:10:44,031
Mara's apple core, from day 92.

330
00:10:44,031 --> 00:10:46,684
Nobody ever came for it.

331
00:10:46,684 --> 00:10:49,166
You put it on the flat stone in the

332
00:10:49,166 --> 00:10:50,177
middle of the sheepfold,

333
00:10:50,177 --> 00:10:53,709
where you laid out everything you had on day 88.

334
00:10:53,709 --> 00:10:57,111
One tin, nine apples, seven matches.

335
00:10:57,644 --> 00:10:59,997
Today your bags hold more than that,

336
00:10:59,997 --> 00:11:02,495
and it still doesn't feel like enough.

337
00:11:02,495 --> 00:11:04,178
You stand inside the wall

338
00:11:04,178 --> 00:11:06,698
and look out over the valley.

339
00:11:06,698 --> 00:11:08,888
The canal, the lock, the ridge.

340
00:11:08,888 --> 00:11:10,149
The mast.

341
00:11:10,149 --> 00:11:12,063
Its ring at the foot is dark.

342
00:11:12,063 --> 00:11:14,564
But beyond it, much farther away,

343
00:11:14,564 --> 00:11:18,152
toward the city, there's a glow on the horizon.

344
00:11:18,152 --> 00:11:19,371
Not the ship.

345
00:11:19,371 --> 00:11:19,980
Lower.

346
00:11:19,980 --> 00:11:20,889
Wider.

347
00:11:21,455 --> 00:11:22,953
Pale, like the bands.

348
00:11:22,953 --> 00:11:25,553
Like lights along a hundred roads,

349
00:11:25,553 --> 00:11:28,603
all switched on together, and left on.

350
00:11:28,993 --> 00:11:30,409
You don't need the plain

351
00:11:30,409 --> 00:11:31,825
figure to draw this one.

352
00:11:31,825 --> 00:11:34,530
The city is waking up first.

353
00:11:34,530 --> 00:11:37,740
On day 204, you go back for the lantern.

354
00:11:37,740 --> 00:11:39,044
It's been at the bottom

355
00:11:39,044 --> 00:11:40,845
of the lock since day 82.

356
00:11:40,845 --> 00:11:42,932
The lock looks tired.

357
00:11:42,932 --> 00:11:45,397
The water is low and brown,

358
00:11:45,397 --> 00:11:48,760
and the old gates leak in long, cold strings.

359
00:11:48,760 --> 00:11:51,727
The hallway is gone from the grass,

360
00:11:51,727 --> 00:11:53,637
but you can still see where it ran,

361
00:11:53,637 --> 00:11:56,791
two pale stripes in the mud, all the way up the hill.

362
00:11:56,791 --> 00:11:58,514
On the walkway of the near gate,

363
00:11:58,514 --> 00:11:59,980
there's nothing.

364
00:11:59,980 --> 00:12:01,117
The can is with you.

365
00:12:01,117 --> 00:12:02,579
At the end of the chamber,

366
00:12:02,579 --> 00:12:05,571
there's an iron ladder set into the stone wall.

367
00:12:05,571 --> 00:12:06,752
You climb down it,

368
00:12:06,752 --> 00:12:08,820
rung by rung, into the cold.

369
00:12:08,820 --> 00:12:09,862
At the bottom,

370
00:12:09,862 --> 00:12:12,331
the water comes up to your knees.

371
00:12:12,331 --> 00:12:14,189
You feel along the mud with your hands,

372
00:12:14,189 --> 00:12:15,201
for a long time.

373
00:12:15,201 --> 00:12:16,941
Long enough that Mara starts

374
00:12:16,941 --> 00:12:19,281
calling down helpful suggestions.

375
00:12:19,736 --> 00:12:21,764
Then your fingers close on a handle.

376
00:12:21,764 --> 00:12:23,945
You lift the lantern out of the mud.

377
00:12:23,945 --> 00:12:25,230
It's black with slime,

378
00:12:25,230 --> 00:12:27,620
and it smells like the bottom of a lock,

379
00:12:27,620 --> 00:12:29,881
which is exactly where it's been.

380
00:12:30,400 --> 00:12:33,112
You climb back up and sit on the walkway,

381
00:12:33,112 --> 00:12:35,299
and clean it with your sleeve.

382
00:12:35,299 --> 00:12:36,820
Then you turn the crank.

383
00:12:37,387 --> 00:12:38,105
Forty turns.

384
00:12:38,105 --> 00:12:40,043
The little whirring sound,

385
00:12:40,043 --> 00:12:43,727
like a very small, very determined insect.

386
00:12:44,390 --> 00:12:46,401
And the lantern lights up.

387
00:12:46,401 --> 00:12:47,071
A small,

388
00:12:47,071 --> 00:12:50,897
yellow, ordinary light, the color of every lamp

389
00:12:50,897 --> 00:12:53,826
in every house before the ship.

390
00:12:53,826 --> 00:12:54,596
Not pale.

391
00:12:54,596 --> 00:12:55,819
Not theirs.

392
00:12:56,578 --> 00:12:57,121
Yours.

393
00:12:57,121 --> 00:13:00,058
Mara looks at it for a long time.

394
00:13:00,528 --> 00:13:01,870
Then she says it's the

395
00:13:01,870 --> 00:13:03,563
most stubborn thing you own.

396
00:13:03,563 --> 00:13:06,745
You decide to take that as a compliment,

397
00:13:06,745 --> 00:13:07,901
for both of you.

398
00:13:07,901 --> 00:13:10,427
On day 206, you reach the narrowboat.

399
00:13:10,427 --> 00:13:12,812
It's exactly where you left it.

400
00:13:12,812 --> 00:13:13,290
Green,

401
00:13:13,290 --> 00:13:16,390
long, with the little chimney on the roof.

402
00:13:16,829 --> 00:13:18,447
Tied to the two iron rings,

403
00:13:18,447 --> 00:13:20,991
with the ropes you retied on day 78.

404
00:13:20,991 --> 00:13:24,006
The apple tree on the towpath is bare.

405
00:13:24,006 --> 00:13:24,992
The ditch in the

406
00:13:24,992 --> 00:13:26,915
field is full of rainwater.

407
00:13:27,434 --> 00:13:29,523
Inside, the two narrow bunks are waiting,

408
00:13:29,523 --> 00:13:32,105
and the camping stove sits on the shelf,

409
00:13:32,105 --> 00:13:34,210
where you left it, still without gas.

410
00:13:34,649 --> 00:13:36,481
Mara unrolls the ledger and

411
00:13:36,481 --> 00:13:38,613
finds the line from day 63.

412
00:13:39,147 --> 00:13:39,681
Boat.

413
00:13:39,681 --> 00:13:41,192
Until the ankle.

414
00:13:41,192 --> 00:13:42,839
And under it,

415
00:13:42,839 --> 00:13:45,947
in her handwriting: not one day longer.

416
00:13:46,369 --> 00:13:48,888
She stamps her foot on the cabin floor,

417
00:13:48,888 --> 00:13:51,615
hard, twice, to prove it still works.

418
00:13:51,615 --> 00:13:53,091
You sleep in the bunks,

419
00:13:53,091 --> 00:13:55,774
with the lantern on the table between you.

420
00:13:55,774 --> 00:13:57,132
It's the nicest night

421
00:13:57,132 --> 00:13:59,276
you've had since the mill.

422
00:13:59,276 --> 00:14:00,466
But in the morning,

423
00:14:00,466 --> 00:14:02,253
you climb onto the roof.

424
00:14:02,755 --> 00:14:03,760
And on the roof,

425
00:14:03,760 --> 00:14:06,424
by the chimney, there's a small marker.

426
00:14:06,846 --> 00:14:09,230
Two circles, joined by a short line.

427
00:14:09,230 --> 00:14:10,161
Glowing.

428
00:14:10,695 --> 00:14:12,930
It wasn't there on day 78.

429
00:14:12,930 --> 00:14:14,058
It's new.

430
00:14:14,544 --> 00:14:16,106
Somebody has been here.

431
00:14:16,106 --> 00:14:17,057
Recently.

432
00:14:17,367 --> 00:14:19,879
Somebody who knew this boat was yours.

433
00:14:19,879 --> 00:14:21,675
You look across the field,

434
00:14:21,675 --> 00:14:23,033
toward the railway.

435
00:14:23,033 --> 00:14:24,119
Along the rails,

436
00:14:24,119 --> 00:14:27,344
the units are standing where they always were.

437
00:14:27,344 --> 00:14:28,963
And every single pair

438
00:14:28,963 --> 00:14:30,613
of circles on them is lit.

439
00:14:30,613 --> 00:14:31,891
Not flickering.

440
00:14:32,264 --> 00:14:34,119
Lit, and staying lit.

441
00:14:34,119 --> 00:14:37,051
On day 208, you walk back to the rails.

442
00:14:37,051 --> 00:14:38,096
The first pair of

443
00:14:38,096 --> 00:14:40,506
circles glows beside your feet.

444
00:14:40,506 --> 00:14:43,209
Then the next one, farther down the track.

445
00:14:43,209 --> 00:14:44,389
And the next.

446
00:14:44,746 --> 00:14:45,676
Toward the city.

447
00:14:45,676 --> 00:14:47,153
Toward the place where you

448
00:14:47,153 --> 00:14:49,450
first saw the can between the rails.

449
00:14:49,450 --> 00:14:51,517
The lights want you again.

450
00:14:51,517 --> 00:14:54,946
On day 31, you stepped off their road.

451
00:14:54,946 --> 00:14:55,717
On day 61,

452
00:14:55,717 --> 00:14:59,441
you climbed away from these very rails.

453
00:14:59,441 --> 00:15:00,669
For a hundred and seventy-seven days,

454
00:15:00,669 --> 00:15:03,571
you have never once followed their lights.

455
00:15:03,976 --> 00:15:04,690
But today,

456
00:15:04,690 --> 00:15:07,417
they're going exactly where you're going.

457
00:15:07,417 --> 00:15:08,577
So you walk.

458
00:15:08,577 --> 00:15:11,366
Both of you, side by side,

459
00:15:11,366 --> 00:15:12,455
on the wooden ties,

460
00:15:12,455 --> 00:15:16,451
with the circles lighting up ahead of you, pair after pair.

461
00:15:16,451 --> 00:15:19,346
It feels like being handed your own map.

462
00:15:19,346 --> 00:15:21,813
Past the place where the can stood.

463
00:15:22,186 --> 00:15:23,415
Past the stretch of stones

464
00:15:23,415 --> 00:15:25,035
where Mara turned her ankle.

465
00:15:25,473 --> 00:15:27,812
The signal hut, with its rain barrel.

466
00:15:27,812 --> 00:15:29,836
The door is still unlocked.

467
00:15:30,355 --> 00:15:31,621
Inside, on the floor,

468
00:15:31,621 --> 00:15:34,160
there's the dent in the dust where you sat

469
00:15:34,160 --> 00:15:35,927
for two nights on day 57,

470
00:15:35,927 --> 00:15:39,237
keeping watch, while Mara's ankle swelled.

471
00:15:39,237 --> 00:15:40,251
Off the rails,

472
00:15:40,251 --> 00:15:42,782
past the bus shelter, the hedge.

473
00:15:42,782 --> 00:15:45,689
The lights don't take you to the stadium.

474
00:15:45,689 --> 00:15:46,955
They take you through

475
00:15:46,955 --> 00:15:49,039
every place you've ever slept.

476
00:15:49,462 --> 00:15:50,150
In reverse.

477
00:15:50,150 --> 00:15:52,042
Like somebody reading your story

478
00:15:52,042 --> 00:15:55,144
back to you, one page at a time.

479
00:15:55,144 --> 00:15:58,394
On day 210, the lights lead you

480
00:15:58,394 --> 00:16:00,199
across the field behind the drain.

481
00:16:00,199 --> 00:16:02,384
The hardware store is still there.

482
00:16:02,384 --> 00:16:05,619
The band that sealed it on day 48 is gone.

483
00:16:05,619 --> 00:16:08,579
The tarp still hangs in the garden yard,

484
00:16:08,579 --> 00:16:09,655
faded and torn,

485
00:16:09,655 --> 00:16:12,173
over two buckets full of old rain.

486
00:16:12,998 --> 00:16:14,910
Mara touches it as she goes past,

487
00:16:14,910 --> 00:16:17,836
the way you'd touch an old friend's shoulder.

488
00:16:17,836 --> 00:16:18,876
Then the drain,

489
00:16:18,876 --> 00:16:22,371
round and cold, with its trickle of water.

490
00:16:22,371 --> 00:16:23,513
Then the road.

491
00:16:23,513 --> 00:16:24,982
Between two units,

492
00:16:24,982 --> 00:16:26,713
at the edge of the tarmac,

493
00:16:26,713 --> 00:16:31,274
there's a small, rusty, empty tin, lying on its side.

494
00:16:31,274 --> 00:16:34,447
The one Mara rolled up the bank on day 33,

495
00:16:34,447 --> 00:16:37,026
to see if the road lit up for tins.

496
00:16:37,026 --> 00:16:38,190
It never did.

497
00:16:38,190 --> 00:16:40,776
Nobody ever picked it up.

498
00:16:40,776 --> 00:16:42,771
The circles light up along it,

499
00:16:42,771 --> 00:16:43,865
toward the bend.

500
00:16:43,865 --> 00:16:45,420
You climb the bank at the

501
00:16:45,420 --> 00:16:46,738
crease on your old map,

502
00:16:46,738 --> 00:16:49,187
the farthest you ever went on day 18.

503
00:16:49,187 --> 00:16:52,332
And from the bend, you can see it.

504
00:16:52,332 --> 00:16:53,478
The gas station.

505
00:16:53,478 --> 00:16:54,785
The canopy.

506
00:16:54,785 --> 00:16:55,601
The pumps.

507
00:16:55,601 --> 00:16:58,125
The shop, with its cracked window.

508
00:16:58,125 --> 00:17:00,847
No band of light around it anymore.

509
00:17:00,847 --> 00:17:01,603
Since day seven,

510
00:17:01,603 --> 00:17:03,531
that station has been dark.

511
00:17:03,857 --> 00:17:04,750
No power.

512
00:17:04,750 --> 00:17:06,356
No pump displays.

513
00:17:06,356 --> 00:17:07,995
No fridge hum.

514
00:17:08,449 --> 00:17:11,276
Tonight, every light in it is on.

515
00:17:11,276 --> 00:17:12,762
The canopy is lit.

516
00:17:12,762 --> 00:17:14,789
The pump displays are glowing.

517
00:17:14,789 --> 00:17:17,150
And through the cracked window,

518
00:17:17,150 --> 00:17:19,368
the shop is bright, as if it's open,

519
00:17:19,368 --> 00:17:22,703
as if any minute now somebody might walk in to buy milk.

520
00:17:23,366 --> 00:17:25,629
You stand at the bend for a long time.

521
00:17:25,629 --> 00:17:26,974
Nobody comes out.

522
00:17:27,316 --> 00:17:29,187
Nothing moves on the forecourt.

523
00:17:29,187 --> 00:17:30,768
The pumps just glow,

524
00:17:30,768 --> 00:17:34,174
patiently, the way the circles glowed along the rails.

525
00:17:34,174 --> 00:17:37,089
As if the whole station has been switched on,

526
00:17:37,089 --> 00:17:39,244
and left on, for you.

527
00:17:39,244 --> 00:17:41,210
Mara takes your hand.

528
00:17:41,210 --> 00:17:42,530
Thirty days.

529
00:17:42,530 --> 00:17:44,302
You walk down toward the light.
